# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kompyle — Example environment variables
#
# NOTHING here is required: with `docker compose up` every value has a working
# default. Copy this file only if you want to change one of them:
#
#   cp .env.example .env          # Docker Compose reads .env automatically
#   cp .env.example .env.local    # for `npm run dev` (Next.js reads .env.local)
#
# AI provider API keys are NOT set here. Kompyle uses a Bring Your Own Key
# (BYOK) model: you enter your Gemini / Groq / OpenRouter / NVIDIA / Anthropic /
# OpenAI key in the "API Keys" dialog of the web app, where it stays in your
# browser's localStorage. The only server-side key is the optional OpenRouter
# fallback below.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─── Docker Compose ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Password of the PostgreSQL container. CHANGE IT before exposing the app on a
# network. It must be set before the first `docker compose up` (the password is
# stored in the database volume afterwards; use `docker compose down -v` to reset).
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=kompyle_dev

# Ports published on your machine (change them if 3000 or 5432 are in use).
# APP_PORT=3000
# DB_PORT=5432

# ─── Database (local development only) ───────────────────────────────────────
# PostgreSQL connection string used by `npm run dev`. Docker Compose sets this
# value for the app container itself. If PostgreSQL is not reachable, the app
# still starts: you can edit and export a CV, but profiles are not saved.
# Start a local database with:  docker compose up -d db
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://kompyle:kompyle_dev@localhost:5432/kompyle"

# ─── Site URL (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public base URL of your deployment, used to build absolute OpenGraph / Twitter
# card image URLs for link previews. Defaults to http://localhost:3000.
# Inlined at BUILD time: with Docker, set it before `docker compose up --build`.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.com

# ─── OpenRouter (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-side fallback key for the OpenRouter provider. Users can still provide
# their own OpenRouter key in the UI; this is only used when no UI key is set.
# Get a key at: https://openrouter.ai/keys
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional headers sent to OpenRouter for attribution / rankings.
# OPENROUTER_SITE_URL=
# OPENROUTER_SITE_NAME=
